videos.script:
The same planner, the same window, and a tenth of the download. {{sizes}}

Tauri does what Electron did with two different parts. The page is drawn by the WebView the system already has. {{engines}} And the part that may touch the computer is written in Rust. {{core}}

So first, Rust itself, and the libraries the system's WebView needs to be built against. {{install}} Then the first build, which stops before it compiles anything, and asks for a name. {{identity}}

Then the door. Lesson 11 wrote it in Node. Here it is a Rust function the page calls by name, with its own tests. {{command}}

And then the build itself. Three packages come out of one command. The program links to the system's browser engine, and its window opens on a screen that is not there. {{build}}

At the end, the two numbers side by side, and what the small one leaves out. {{trade}}
